# EVERY LAYER ANY DOCUMENT DECLARES, WHATEVER IT WENT ON TO SAY ABOUT IT. One row per
# (filing, layer): the roster, before any of the vectors decide whether they have an entry for it.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ EVERY OTHER RELATION IN THIS DIRECTORY IS A FILTER ON THIS ONE, AND UNTIL NOW THE THING
#    BEING FILTERED HAD NO NAME. `layers/demand.sqlc` keeps the layers with a stated demand,
#    `layers/nameplate.sqlc` those with a stated amount, `layers/absorber.sqlc` those whose
#    taxonomy a reader has mapped. Each is correct, and each is a sparse reading of a population
#    that was never written down -- so five files reached into `pm.layer` for existence alone,
#    projecting no column of it, because there was nothing to compose.
#
# ⛔ EXISTENCE IS NOT A COLUMN, AND THAT IS WHY THIS FILE LOOKS EMPTY. It carries the key and
#   nothing else on purpose. A caller wanting a layer's demand composes layers/demand.sqlc; a
#   caller asking only whether the layer IS composes this. `composition/parts.sqlc` and
#   `checks/local_part_dangles.sqlc` ask exactly that question, once positively and once as its
#   complement, and neither could name what it was asking of.
#
# ⭐ RUN IT ALONE AND IT IS THE DENOMINATOR FOR EVERY COVERAGE FIGURE IN THE REPOSITORY. Any
#   "so many of the lumpy layers" needs its denominator from somewhere, and this is where.
-- pm:Stack/pm:layer, keyed and nothing more.
SELECT l.filing, l.layer
FROM pm.layer l
